    "abstract": "Swin Transformer is a hierarchical vision Transformer whose representation is computed with shifted windows: self-attention is limited to non-overlapping local windows while allowing cross-window connections, giving linear complexity in image size. It serves as a general-purpose backbone, achieving 87.3% ImageNet-1K top-1, 58.7 box AP / 51.1 mask AP on COCO test-dev and 53.5 mIoU on ADE20K val.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Self-attention within non-overlapping M x M windows gives complexity linear in the number of tokens.",
      "Alternating regular and shifted window partitions in consecutive blocks creates cross-window connections efficiently.",
      "A hierarchical design with patch merging produces multi-scale feature maps suitable for dense prediction.",
      "Swin-T reaches 81.3% ImageNet-1K top-1 with 28M parameters.",
      "Swin-L achieves 58.7 box AP and 51.1 mask AP on COCO test-dev and 53.5 mIoU on ADE20K val."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
